From: Harvi654 <202698022+Harvi654@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msi: Keep measured required attr26 selections after costing.

AI-assisted (Codex), original code; LGPL-2.1-or-later.

Windows v14 stable preparation returns success for Absent on an attr26
Local child without deselecting it. Unknown/Absent targets are not extended.
Do not generalize UIDisallowAbsent to all
attributes: existing package.c lyra (attr16) must still accept Absent.
Shared v14 stable before/after/publish assertions; RULE_API. Maintenance
and other combinations keep the old behavior.

--- a/dlls/msi/install.c
+++ b/dlls/msi/install.c
@@ -1030,6 +1030,8 @@
         BOOL required = feature->Attributes == (msidbFeatureAttributesFollowParent |
             msidbFeatureAttributesDisallowAdvertise | msidbFeatureAttributesUIDisallowAbsent);
 
+        if (after_cost && iState == INSTALLSTATE_ABSENT && required &&
+            feature->ActionRequest == INSTALLSTATE_LOCAL) return ERROR_SUCCESS;
         if ((iState == INSTALLSTATE_SOURCE && required) ||
             (after_cost && iState == INSTALLSTATE_ADVERTISED && required &&
              feature->ActionRequest == INSTALLSTATE_LOCAL))
